A||N||4||FieroMaster88||Indy Advice!  Begenning restoration!||||5||
Z||000000||FieroMaster88||01-09-2001||02:19 AM||||Hello all,<P>I am finally begenning to restore my Indy Fiero.  I was just wondering how to do a couple things.  <P>I need to know how to refinish the rims.  What do I use to strip them?  What paint to repaint them with???  <P>Also, what to look for?  I want to know what I unique things I should look for while taking her apart.  <P>And last, where is a good place to get parts for a Indy???  I need the front facia, decal kit, leather doorpulls, steering wheel, shifter and a fender badge.  <P>Thanks and any advice would help.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">  <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster86<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles<BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||01-09-2001||02:32 AM||||To refinish wheels, Use Permatex spray-on gasket remover. It will remove the paint. To paint the wheels I use Krylon Rust Tough. To seal the wheel, Duplicolor make a spray-on clear urethane wheel paint. If you do a seach (I think it's in the archives) under my name you'll find the products I used to refinish my GT style wheels.<P>Found the thread:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20001206-1-002367.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20001206-1-002367.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||01-09-2001||09:07 AM||||A company called Phoenix Graphix has the decal kit. $219 for everything!<P> <A HREF="http://www.phoenixgraphix.com/gm/1984if.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.phoenixgraphix.com/gm/1984if.htm</A> <P>The 85 GT, and 86-87 SE noses are the same as the Indy. You can find these in a lot of places. Some of the guys on here that sell parts may have them, i.e.- Fiero Factory, Fiero Warehouse, FieroDave, etc...<P>The door pulls on my Indy have been restored by FieroDave. The previous owner had this done. He may be able to do the steering wheel and shifter too, I'm not sure. Mr. Mike's makes leather seats and stuff for Fiero's. He may have them too.<P>Fender badges... Well, I don't know. I need one too. Looks like salvage yards for these if you can find them! I'll keep my eyes open for extras as I am looking for one for me.<P>Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 01-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||01-09-2001||11:00 AM||||There is some indy stuff on ebay right now.  I saw some repro stickers, fender badges, fascia emblems.  Thought you might like to know.<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=539034731" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=539034731</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=539036087" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=539036087</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||4
